put.description:
 Updates the bank details of an employee

 For an employee to be included in a pay run and to be paid, they must have at least one bank account on their master record.
 Multiple bank accounts and payment splits can be assigned to an employee. If multiple bank accounts exist for an employee, the last one must be set as “Remainder” to ensure any surplus funds once all the other rules for preceding bank accounts have been processed.

 This PUT must include all bank accounts, so edit/add/delete a bank account requires all bank accounts to be set as you want them
 <pre>
{
         "notPaidViaEFT": false,
         "paymentAccounts": [
         {
             "bankAccount": {
                 "accountName": "Marg Acc",
                 "bank": "ANZ",
                 "bsb": "012012",
                 "accountNumber": "1234567",
                 "reference": "Wife Deposit"
             },
             "paySplit": {
                 "type": "Fixed",
                 "amount": "350"
             },
             "sortOrder": 0,
 },
 {
             "bankAccount": {
                 "accountName": "John Acc",
                 "bank": "ANZ",
                 "bsb": "012012",
                 "accountNumber": "7654321",
                 "reference": "Main Account"
             },
             "paySplit": {
                 "type": "Remainder",
                 "amount": null
             },
             "sortOrder": 1,
         }
         ]
     }
 </pre>

